{"id": "unknown-2026-08-29-001", "date": "2026-08-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Higher LNG prices, supply shortages compound Bangladesh gas crisis", "content": "The deepening gas and electricity crises in Bangladesh have been compounded by a sharp rise in global LNG prices and supply shortages coinciding with high power demand. \nIndustrial production has been severely hit, with 70 per cent of the production capacity of gas-dependent factories staying unutilised, pressuring the export sector. \nThe energy crunch is no longer confined to power-intensive industries. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/higher-lng-prices-supply-shortages-compound-bangladesh-gas-crisis-313033-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-29-002", "date": "2026-08-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Can Bangladesh’s fiscal reset put growth on a faster track?", "content": "Bangladesh is set to shift its fiscal year from July-June to April-March, with FY2027-28 a nine-month transition before April 2028. \nA five-member committee will identify constitutional, legal and financial-system changes needed to implement the calendar. \nAn April start could create a three-month dry-season window for faster construction, but experts warn old bottlenecks may persist. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-bangladesh-s-fiscal-reset-put-growth-on-a-faster-track--313025-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-29-003", "date": "2026-08-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["growth", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia’s ASEAN apparel exports rise but trail Asia-Pacific growth", "content": "Cambodia’s apparel exports to ASEAN rose 5.5 per cent to $157.242 million in H1 2026.\nGrowth outpaced the 2.1 per cent rise in worldwide apparel exports but trailed Asia-Pacific’s 6.8 per cent expansion.\nASEAN held 10.4 per cent of Cambodia’s Asia-Pacific apparel exports and nearly 1.7 per cent of worldwide shipments.\nT-shirts, jerseys and coats grew; trousers, shorts and shirts declined.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/cambodia-s-asean-apparel-exports-rise-but-trail-asia-pacific-growth-312946-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
